s done is that  they've banked their hubs what this  means is that for the most part all  their flights arrive in two part at  roughly the same time for example on any  given Wednesday in the fall the  Philadelphia flight will arrive at 11:14  a.m. than the Atlanta flight at 11:17  a.m. the DC one at 11:29 and the  Nashville flight at 11:45 then at 12:40  the flight to Denver leaves then at  12:45 the one in Las Vegas at 1:00 the  one to San Francisco and  10 the flight to Los Angeles this way  nobody has to wait for longer than two  hours to connect almost every flight  American operates in and out of DFW  falls into one of their 10 daily banks  this is how the airline gets those  connecting passengers by offering  shorter connection times nearby Dallas  Love Field is Southwest Airlines main  hub but it operates in an entirely  different way  it just has planes arriving and leaving  at a consistent average of about 8 to 12  flights per hour all day long and  there's a good reason for this Southwest  is a budget airline bank tubs are  significantly more expensive to run  because they require more resources the  airline needs to have enough equipment  people and gates to turn around all  their planes at the same time if the  planes came in at a smooth paste all the  people and equipment could be used  continuously but at a bank tub the  airline still needs to pay for the  people and equipment during the downtime  between the banks if a plane leaves  Philadelphia bound for DC at 9:30 with a  9:00 to 10:00 a.m. pink it will arrive  around 10 a.m. but it will have to wait  to leave until about 11:15 to time its  arrival with the 11:45 to 12:45 Bank  planes cost money whether they're in the  air or sitting on the ground  so having planes wait around a time with  banks cost money too this is why a  budget airline will never schedule their  planes to sit on the ground during the  day for more than an hour once a plane  lands it immediately loads up and takes  off again as 